From: mattryznar <ryznarmat@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 17:24:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] Iskra: SVM nested paging self-test (hypervisor step 2)

A 32-bit paged guest runs in its own guest-physical address space through
4-level nested page tables. It writes guest memory the host can read back,
faults to the host on an unmapped address (NPF exit for 0x5000), and after the
host maps a page there and resumes, completes with the new value.
---
